	<text xml:lang="la">
		<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" subtype="metadata" n="1">Wie aus unten <ref target="file12156">Nr. 2109</ref>, 1, hervorgeht, war <persName ref="p8073" cert="high">Cousin</persName> bei <persName ref="p1278" cert="high">Johannes Gast</persName> in <placeName ref="l28" cert="high">Basel</placeName> zu Besuch.</note>
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>S[alutem] p[lurimam].</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l922">Friburgo</placeName> <placeName ref="l922">Brisgoiae</placeName> per <placeName ref="l28">Basileam</placeName> in <placeName ref="l631">Burgundiam</placeName> rediens,<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2"><persName ref="p8073">Cousin</persName> lebte in <placeName ref="l356">Nozeroy</placeName> (<placeName ref="l3422">Dép. Jura</placeName>), wo er sich Ende 1535 niedergelassen hatte.</note> vir clarissime, <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>quum <persName ref="p1278">Gastius</persName> noster nuncium<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Unbekannt.</note> <placeName ref="l587">Tigurum</placeName> se cras<note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a">cras <hi>über der Zeile nachgetragen.</hi></note><note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Der Brief, dem ein Geschenk für <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> beigelegt war (s. unten Anm. 11), verließ <placeName ref="l28">Basel</placeName> erst am 14. März 1545 oder kurz darauf; s. unten <ref target="file12156">Nr. 2109</ref>, 1-3.</note> missurum diceret, et me, si quid <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>vellem, rogaret, nolui committere, ut is sine meis literis abiret mei in te animi <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>significatricibus, tametsi de mea adversum te observantia nihil te dubitare <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>credam.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Pro benignitate autem tua, qua me quam plurimis annis perpetuo complecteris, <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>tibi gratias ago immortales.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Cuius quidem nuper in aperienda candide <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>mihi tua de eucharistia sententia specimen<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5"><persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> verlorene Antwort auf <persName ref="p8073">Cousins</persName> Brief, in dem er auf <persName ref="p8073">Cousins</persName> Anfrage seine Meinung über das Abendmahl darlegt hatte; s. <bibl source="b17">HBBW XIV</bibl>, <ref target="file11974">Nr. 1927</ref> und Anm. 15.</note> quoque praebuisti.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Utinam is <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>sim, mi <persName ref="p495">Bullingere</persName>, qui aliquando non ingratum me declarare possim!</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Voluntas, <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>ita me deus amet, nunquam deest; quam si re ipsa factis pręstare non potero<note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Röm 7, 16</ref></cit>.</note> - <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>cum maior sis, quam quo conatus nostri adspirare valent -<pb type="edition" next="178"/> conatum tamen <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>laudabis, quando in magnis, ut ille<note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7"><persName ref="p19941">Sextus Propertius (Properz)</persName> aus <placeName ref="l3430">Assisi</placeName> (ca. 50 bis ca. 15 v. Chr).</note> inquit, vel voluisse sat est<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8">Vgl. <hi><persName ref="p19941">Properz</persName>,</hi> Elegiae, 2, 10, 5; in Adagia, 2,S. 55 (<bibl>ASD</bibl> II/4 184, Nr. 1755).</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Mi <persName ref="p495">Bullingere</persName>, <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>cura, quoad potes, ut valeas, sicque existimes nihil nobis tua valetudine <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>iucundius, nihil ęque gratius adnunciari posse.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l28">Basileę</placeName>, 4. idus martii <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>anno christiano 1545, praepropere, ut vides.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p1278">Gastio</persName> commisi ad te <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>munus<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Ein Hemd aus einem Mischgewebe mit Seide; s. unten <ref target="file12225">Nr. 2178</ref>, 3.</note>; id ut boni consulas, etiam atque etiam rogo.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Amicis omnibus s[alutem] p[lurimam], <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>imprimis <persName ref="p8171">Bibliandro</persName> et <persName ref="p1283">Guesnero</persName>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z17"/>Ex animo tuus <persName ref="p8073">Gilbertus Cognatus <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>Nozeręus</persName><note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>Ansonsten bezeichnet sich <persName ref="p8073">Cousin</persName> als</hi> Nozerenus.</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Domino <persName ref="p495">Henrico Bullingero</persName>, <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>verę theologię ac christia<lb xml:id="p2z3"/>nismi vindici incomparabili, <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>domino et praeceptori suo <lb xml:id="p2z5"/>observando.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p2z6"/><placeName ref="l587">Tiguri</placeName>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
